From ebd4a17d578e0f98d7fbe5bbf0afe4e56de75409 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stew Forster <stew675@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 08:59:46 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 19/28] WIP indexer: fuse the prefill indexer relu + head-sum

The qwen4exp prefill score chain is mul_mat -> relu -> reshape_4d -> head views +
adds (+ optional 4-D bias), and the relu sits BEFORE the reshape (the L2a memory
win).  A fused kernel recomputes the relu from the pre-relu scores and sums the heads
in graph order, reading the block scores once instead of H times.

Matcher anchored at the RELU, accepting the optional following RESHAPE; is_slice uses
the reshape's strides but view_src == relu, because ggml collapses a view-of-a-view
to the relu root.  Bit-identical: fmaxf + the same left-to-right add order.

Gates (qwen4exp IQ4_NL, gfx1151): width probe W=1..8 + row0 268e0673300b7a33
unchanged / PASS; plain == draft-mtp byte-identical (984263fb8e0f).

-b/-ub 4096 -n 0 -r 3: pp8192 flat (1293.0 vs 1293.2), pp32768 1241.9 -> 1264.5
(+1.8 %).  Kill switch GGML_CUDA_DISABLE_IDX_RELU_SUM=1; gated RDNA3_5 like the
reference.
